 "title": "Уход с праздника  (Leaving the Party)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "kostya": "Костя",
  "nastya": "Настя"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "At the party, Nastya has had enough and heads for the door, and Kostya stops her. Listen to it in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Пока.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "О, уже уходишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Ага. Как-то здесь невесело.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Подожди. Я...",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Что?",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go through what they said.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Пока.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Bye.' The word poka is the casual goodbye; literally it means 'for now'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "О, уже уходишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, you're leaving already?' Russian uses ukhodish, 'you're going away', for leaving a place, and uzhe means 'already'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Ага. Как-то здесь невесело.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Yeah. It's kind of dull here.' The word nevesyolo is ne, 'not', plus vesyolo, 'cheerful', and aga is a casual 'yeah'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Подожди. Я...",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Wait. I...' The word podozhdi is how you'd say 'wait' to a friend; to a stranger you'd say podozhdite.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Что?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What?' In Russian chto means 'what', and in speech it sounds like 'shto'. And the goodbye again.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Пока.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "О, уже уходишь?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Ага. Как-то здесь невесело.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "kostya",
   "t": "Подожди. Я...",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Что?",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Kostya has stopped Nastya, and now he has to say it. You'd say podozhdi to a friend, and podozhdite to anyone you call vy. See you next time!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Пока!",
   "gap": 0.3
  }
 ],
